      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>20CM BGL 5.2M N GP 43M SW FENC

Elevation 772.485 m
20CM BGL; 5.2M NORTH OF A GP
IN THE VILLAGE OF CARBON; 42.6 M SW OF THE BALL DIAMOND FENCE</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1117726022">
          <groundspeak:date>2022-08-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP517 Carbon [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Camping in the main campground this week, so I convinced my family to join my growing cap addiction and go for this one. Thanks to a couple of good past pictures we pretty much knew where to dig. The woman in the nearest trailer to GZ seemed interested and accepting of our nuttiness. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lots of fun on my birthday, thanks for another cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684672315">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP517 - Carbon&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time we went east!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Once we figured out where to go and how to get there, it was pretty quick. A swipe from a paper towel was all it needed! The geodog enjoyed her quick &quot;escape&quot; from the vehicle to eat some grass. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_dead.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Pretty scarred up cap. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_sad.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684653997">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP517 - Carbon - we picked up a rock in the brakes near here and announced our arrival with a huge screech, thankfully no one was around to notice.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680743191">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1298988">dronnord</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 517 Carbon&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;N51° 29.018 W113° 08.793  Elev = 773  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What a quaint little town. Loved the campsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks OFTH For bringing me here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;7 PM time to get moving &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5/6 for the day&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="679546358">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-19T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="440625">Everhollow</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP517 – Carbon

N 51° 29.016 W 113° 08.789&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our experience at this cap had us giggling most of the way back to the car.  We had done a little digging to locate the cap and were about to fill in the hole when we noticed a fellow with surveyor equipment on the wrong side of the fence, the side with the guard post.  We wondered if by some bizarre chance he would be looking for BCP517 – Carbon, just when we were there.   Sure enough he was!  And not for geocaching but for his work.  So these shiny brass caps actually serve a purpose other than logging GC43F3!   &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Thank you so much for keeping this cache going outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
